se\\n  maxSwitches: number;     // switch limit per cycle\\n  phaseModelMap: PhaseModelMap;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Add config toggle to `lib/semblr-config.ts`\\nAdd `multiModelRouting` to the SemblrConfig interface:\\n- `enabled`: boolean, default `false` (opt-in)\\n- `maxSwitches`: number, default `3`\\n- `phaseModelMap`: PhaseModelMap with the Ollama-Cloud hardcoded map\\n\\n### 4. Add state fields to `lib/state.ts`\\nAdd to the conversation state:\\n- `switchCounter: number` (tracks switches per cycle, resets each cycle)\\n- `currentPhase: PhaseName | null` (current reported phase)\\n- `pendingModelSwitch: string | null` (model to switch to at agent_end)\\n\\n### 5. Create `lib/resolve-model-id.ts` (NEW FILE)\\n```typescript\\n// Resolves Ollama-Cloud model IDs like \\\"glm-5.2:cloud\\\" to actual provider model IDs\\n// For MVP: strip \\\":cloud\\\" suffix, keep the base name for ollama provider\\nexport function resolveModelId(modelId: string): { provider: string; model: string };\\n```\\n- If modelId contains \\\":cloud\\\", strip it and use \\\"ollama\\\" provider\\n- Otherwise, pass through as-is\\n- Write unit tests alongside\\n\\n### 6. Create `lib/phase-model-map.ts` (NEW FILE)\\nExport the hardcoded MVP phase→model map (from comment #2 on the issue):\\n```typescript\\nexport const MVP_PHASE_MODEL_MAP: PhaseModelMap = {\\n  thinking: null,           // stay on default model for thinking\\n  executing: \\\"glm-5.2:cloud\\\",\\n  stuck: \\\"kimi-k2.6:cloud\\\",\\n  reporting: \\\"gemma4:12b:cloud\\\",\\n  reviewing: \\\"deepseek-v4-pro:cloud\\\",  \\n  verifying: \\\"deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\\\",\\n};\\n```\\nAlso export a function `getModelForPhase(phase: PhaseName, map: PhaseModelMap): string | null`.\\n\\n### 7. Write unit tests\\nFor `resolveModelId` and `getModelForPhase`. Follow existing test patterns.\\n\\n### 8. Verify\\n```bash\\nnpx tsc --noEmit   # typecheck\\nnpx vitest run     # run tests\\n```\\n\\nWrite all findings/decisions to `/home/vedat/wo